{
  "id": "permeability",
  "title": "Permeability",
  "description": "Electromagnetism and formation of magnetic fields. Calculate permeability and relative permeability of materials.",
  "type": "calculator-table",
  "components": [
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "content": "# Permeability Calculator\n\nPermeability is the ability to support formation of magnetic fields in a material.\n\n## Key Constants\n\n- **Permeability of free space (µ₀)**: 4π × 10⁻⁷ H/m ≈ 1.257 × 10⁻⁶ H/m\n\n## Formula\n\n**Relative Permeability**: µᵣ = µ / µ₀\n\nwhere:\n- µᵣ = relative permeability (dimensionless)\n- µ = permeability of the medium (H/m)\n- µ₀ = permeability of free space (H/m)"
    },
    {
      "type": "calculator",
      "inputs": [
        {
          "id": "permeability",
          "label": "Permeability (µ)",
          "type": "number",
          "unit": "H/m",
          "defaultValue": 0.00000125663753
        }
      ],
      "outputs": [
        {
          "id": "relative_permeability",
          "label": "Relative Permeability (µᵣ)",
          "formula": "inputs.permeability / 1.25663753e-6",
          "unit": "dimensionless",
          "format": "decimal"
        }
      ]
    },
